		<TD>
			<CENTER><FONT FACE="Arial, Helvetica"><B>JOINING THE HIGH PLANES AMBASSADORS</B></CENTER><BR>

			<FONT SIZE="-1">We look for quality players whose objective is to have FUN while working their way up to the highest levels of the game. Teamwork, a sense of camaraderie, and a respect for our fellow citizens of Norrath are a must!<BR><BR>

			The High Planes Ambassadors accept characters from all classes and races above level 14.  However, the guild keeps a balanced ratio of players across all levels at any given time; therefore the amount of time for an application to be reviewed may vary from time to time, based on the level of the applicant.  As a general rule of thumb, the process from application to invitation can take less than a week for higher level characters, but often longer than two weeks for lower level characters.   A guild representative will generally get in contact with an applicant right away to let them know what the anticipated period of time may be given the current distribution of levels.<BR><BR>

			<B><I>Applying for Membership.</I></B> Applicants need two sponsors from the High Planes Ambassadors to join The best way to join the High Planes Ambassadors is to group up with a Full Member who can become your first sponsor. (If you have grouped with or know a Full Member of the guild, then you already have a sponsor!) Once you have a sponsor, fill out the application below, and an interview with a High Council member will be arranged -- they may become your second sponsor. If you can't seem to hook up with a full member, contact a High Council member who will direct someone your way or will make other arrangements -- but having a primary Full Member sponsor is definitely the best way to go.<BR><BR>

			<B><I>Provisional and Full Membership.</I></B> Upon successful completion of the interview, applicants are brought into the guild as Provisional Members, during which time an informal review process continues, assuring the Provisional Member of compatibility with the guild, and vice versa. Provisional Members change to Full Member status in approximately one month; variables that affect this period of time include amount of time played; degree of mutual encouragement and support of other guild members; and general alignment to guild policies and principles.   Provisional Members enjoy all of the same support and participation in the guild as Full Members, the only difference being that Full Members may bring more than one alternate character into the guild and may sponsor other applicants.<BR><BR>

			<B><I>Secondary Characters.</I></B> Many of our members have more than one character in the guild. Full Members can bring multiple characters of any level into the guild by sending a tell to any officer while playing on their primary character. Secondary characters must also fill out an application in order to be maintained on the guild website, using their primary character as "reference". (Enter your normal login and password if you are signing up a secondary character.)<BR><BR></FONT>

